emote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator-authorized default 2026-09-07: choose the narrow checker extension, not a broad audit ticket. Rationale: the ticket describes a specific gate blind spot and the documented-best-practice default is to implement the smallest diagnosable behavior that prevents recurrence; any broader audit can be discovered separately if implementation reveals additional latent flakes. Acceptance target: check_wall_clock_asserts should flag equality/inequality assertions comparing read_bytes()/read_text() output from separate artifact paths when the test lacks a frozen clock, while avoiding existing frozen-clock/irrelevant comparisons.","timestamp":1788795637639518001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review did not reach a claimable PASS after the allowed retry. First run blocked on missing standard AC/verification; I revised the description with standard AC and a testing proof. Retry was INDETERMINATE due provider/search failure: DDGSException 'No results found.' Per operator workflow, skipping this ticket rather than forcing claim.","timestamp":1788796388063049001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator-authorized default 2026-09-07: after plan-review findings, choose a syntactic proxy rule for the existing test-only AST checker rather than product-code timestamp provenance analysis. Rationale: the checker can deterministically detect unfrozen equality/inequality comparisons of different read_bytes/read_text receivers and produce a reviewable warning; attempting to infer embedded wall-clock metadata from product code would be broad, brittle, and outside this lint's architecture. Also correcting the test path to tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py.","timestamp":1788803934991750001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Stopped after genuine plan-review FAIL following one findings-driven description revision. Latest blocking finding verbatim: The rule fires on every cross-artifact read_bytes()/read_text() equality comparison regardless of whether the artifact actually embeds a timestamp, but the only escape is freezing _now_iso/utc_now_iso — which is unavailable for tests comparing timestamp-free artifacts — and a new suppression marker is explicitly out of scope. The plan does not estimate this false-positive surface, yet the lint runs in make verify. Suggested fix: Add a quick survey of current read_bytes()/read_text() equality asserts under tests/** to the plan (count + whether each embeds a clock seam), and either confirm all newly-flagged cases genuinely embed timestamps or reconsider allowing a minimal inline suppression comment for proven timestamp-free comparisons. Advisory also requested defining receiver identity/tracking scope.","timestamp":1788805991176456001}],"created_at":1787941522681366001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cfb0149b-f191-45a8-bf15-24398ed396c4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c49a-225d-2bc0-4478"},{"link_uuid":"ad71b828-f10d-4a0b-9de6-714579a90d53","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e057-1f93-5328-4c25"},{"link_uuid":"964e7f31-b2e2-4bc7-b04a-5af48be5f51f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"395a-6e9e-8c63-4a5e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while fixing bug `c49a-225d-2bc0-4478` (`perplexed-jeanlike-kakarikis`). `check_wall_clock_asserts` missed an indirect wall-clock flake: `test_narrow_operation_persists_the_same_bytes_as_the_legacy_sequence` compared bytes from two independently saved `BindingStore` files. Each save stamps `created_at` / `updated_at` through `BindingLifecycle.bind_confirm` -> `_now_iso`; crossing a one-second boundary made the serialized bytes differ even though the test had no direct elapsed-time assertion.\n\n## Prior BLOCKs addressed\n\nPrior reviews correctly rejected a blanket cross-artifact `read_bytes()` / `read_text()` equality rule because timestamp-free byte comparisons also exist and the variable-assignment shape had not been surveyed. This plan narrows the detector and adds a reason-required local escape.\n\n## False-positive survey\n\nDirect call-vs-call equality under `tests/**` currently appears in these cases:\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py`: the motivating timestamp flake; already freezes `_now_iso` and should not need an escape.\n- Timestamp-free/deterministic comparisons needing exemption or explicit reason markers if newly flagged: `tests/integration/test_comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py`, `tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_corpus.py`, `tests/unit/test_build_provenance_fixture_scale.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_snapshot.py`, `tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_escape_index.py`, `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`, and `tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py`.\n\nVariable-mediated byte/text comparisons currently found under `tests/**` are same-receiver re-read/idempotency checks, not cross-receiver comparisons. Examples: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py`, `test_binding_baseline.py`, `test_binding_repository.py`, `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py`, `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py`, and `tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py`. The implementation must therefore resolve variable sources and exempt variable-vs-direct comparisons when both sides refer to the same receiver expression.\n\n## Decision / Scope\n\nImplement a syntactic, conservative proxy rule in `scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py`; do not attempt whole-product timestamp provenance analysis.\n\nRules:\n\n- Fire on `assert left.read_bytes() == right.read_bytes()` / `!=`, and equivalent `read_text()` comparisons, only when the two receiver expressions are structurally different.\n- Fire on variables assigned from `read_bytes()` / `read_text()` receivers and later compared with equality/inequality in the same test function only when both compared sides resolve to file-read receivers and those receiver expressions are structurally different.\n- Do not fire when the enclosing test freezes `_now_iso` or `utc_now_iso` via `monkeypatch.setattr`.\n- Do not fire on same-receiver comparisons, including variable-vs-direct re-reads of the same receiver expression.\n- Add a narrow inline escape marker, `# timing: artifact-equality — <reason>`, covering the assert line or the line directly above. A non-empty reason is mandatory. It is only for reviewed deterministic/timestamp-free artifact comparisons or same-source copy checks.\n- Annotate existing timestamp-free direct comparisons newly flagged by the checker with specific reasons; leave the motivating frozen-clock test unescaped.\n\nFinding text should say this is a transitive wall-clock flake proxy and recommend freezing the clock, asserting semantic fields, or using the reason-required escape only for proven timestamp-free artifacts.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Product-code timestamp provenance analysis.\n- A broad config allowlist or force-style bypass.\n- Auditing beyond the survey above and the checker's test suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py` has a RED-first test proving direct equality/inequality between different `read_bytes()` / `read_text()` receivers is flagged without a clock freeze or escape.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py` has a RED-first test proving variable-assignment comparisons from different file-content receivers are flagged.\n- [ ] Contrast tests prove same-receiver direct comparisons, same-receiver variable-vs-direct re-reads, `_now_iso` / `utc_now_iso` freezes, and `artifact-equality` escapes are not flagged.\n- [ ] Escape tests cover both marker placements: assert line and directly preceding line; blank-reason markers still fire.\n- [ ] Existing upper-bound wall-clock assertion behavior and hang-guard / CI-skip escapes remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Existing timestamp-free comparisons in the survey either remain unflagged by same-receiver/frozen-clock logic or are annotated with specific `artifact-equality` reasons.\n- [ ] Verification: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py` exits zero, followed before push by `make verify` with the worktree venv on `PATH` and GIT_CONFIG_* unset.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py","reason":"extend heuristic for transitive timestamp-sensitive file-content equality and its reason-required escape"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py","reason":"RED/GREEN coverage for transitive timestamp-sensitive comparisons and escapes"},{"path":"tests/**/*.py","reason":"annotate any existing timestamp-free direct artifact comparisons newly flagged by the checker with specific escape reasons"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","395a-6e9e-8c63-4a5e"],["relates_to","e057-1f93-5328-4c25"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"76bc1529-b064-4213-95f2-22b9a5004967","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f8c6-6ab3-ca81-4d30","ticket_type":"task","title":"check_wall_clock_asserts misses transitive timestamp flakes (byte-equality of independently-timestamped saves)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["550ce5f6-4614-4836-bf2f-dd085d2c577c","cceca3dd-dddd-494b-922a-6df599b068c7","49052427-d34a-469d-b01d-b1181d1d9497","ad71b828-f10d-4a0b-9de6-714579a90d53","fc9fb99f-578c-4f91-abcc-dbd0bdfad203","3